(unchanged, 2891 jobs). No code changes — pure analysis.\",\"id\":\"83\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 29): DEEP ANALYSIS of plaquette induction (§8.11.35). KEY FINDING: The σ twist (temporal link inversion at the interface) is the SOLE obstacle. The factorization B = B₁·B₁ reduces the integral to ∫ F·F(σ) dμ⁰. Without σ, trivially ≥0. With σ, NOT necessarily ≥0 for general f (counterexample: ℤ/3ℤ). CONCLUSION: Lüscher approach integrates out temporal links FIRST, avoiding σ twist. Build GREEN (unchanged, 2891 jobs). No code changes — pure analysis.\",\"id\":\"84\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 30): CRITICAL FINDING — the axiom transferMatrixPositivity_axiom was FALSE as stated (with dependsOnlyOnPosInterface). Counterexample: β=0, f(g)=Im Tr(g) on a temporal interface link gives ∫ f(g)·f(g⁻¹) dg = -∫ (Im Tr(g))² dg < 0. FIX APPLIED: defined dependsOnlyOnPosSpatialInterface (excludes temporal interface links μ=0 at t=0), proved it implies dependsOnlyOnPosInterface, weakened the axiom + all downstream lemmas. Build GREEN (2890 jobs). 0 sorries, 0 new custom axioms. Documented in §8.11.36.\",\"id\":\"85\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 31): KEY FINDINGS for proving the weakened axiom. (1) β² CONVENTION: plaquetteContribution = β*(1-(1/N)Re Tr), so Boltzmann factor = exp(-β²*∑(1-(1/N)Re Tr)), which is ALWAYS ≤1 and symmetric in β→-β. Character expansion uses c=β²/N≥0 for ALL β — NO need to add β≥0 hypothesis. (2) σ DISAPPEARS FROM g: with dependsOnlyOnPosSpatialInterface, g(V⁺,σ(u⁰))=g(V⁺,u⁰) because f doesn't depend on u⁰_t and σ only inverts u⁰_t. (3) PROOF STRUCTURE: integral reduces to ∫_{u⁰_s}∫_{U⁺}∫_{V⁺} g(U⁺,u⁰_s)·g(V⁺,u⁰_s)·J(U⁺,V⁺,u⁰_s) dμ where J=∫_{u⁰_t} K dμ⁰_t. (4) J needs diagonal char expansion (Lüscher mechanism — the hard part). (5) Shared-variable character_expansion_nonneg lemma WRITTEN but has Mathlib API issues. Lemma is COMMENTED OUT in PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean (build GREEN, 2892 jobs). See §8.11.37.\",\"id\":\"86\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 32): PROVED character_expansion_nonneg_shared (shared-variable positivity lemma, PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean:1196) + reflectSite_interface_self (ReflectionPositivity.lean:238). KEY FIX for coercion mismatch: simp only [← RCLike.ofReal_eq_complex_ofReal] before rw [integral_ofReal]. 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms. Build GREEN (2972 jobs). See §8.11.37.\",\"id\":\"87\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-05 session 33): PROVED COMPLETE σ-disappears-from-g CHAIN (step 1 of proof strategy). SIX lemmas, all 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms, build GREEN (2972 jobs): (1) sigmaInterface_spatial_fixed (TransferMatrix.lean:1870) — σ fixes spatial interface links (μ≠0) via reflectSite_interface_self. (2) extendLinkVariable_merge_sigma_agree (TransferMatrix.lean:1891) — extended merged configs agree on pos+spatial-interface links. (3) f_sigma_invisible (TransferMatrix.lean:1918) — dependsOnlyOnPosSpatialInterface → f ignores σ. (4) wilsonActionOSPositive_congr (TransferMatrix.lean:1935) — S⁺ only reads positive-site links (helper). (5) osPositiveOfPosInterface_sigma_invariant (TransferMatrix.lean:1968) — S⁺ ignores σ. (6) g_posInterface_sigma_invisible (TransferMatrix.lean:1983) — MAIN LEMMA: g(mergePosInterface(V⁺,σ(u⁰))) = g(mergePosInterface(V⁺,u⁰)). KEY TECHNICAL: AddVector.addVector = addVectorPeriodic T L by rfl (instance projection reducible); simp only [hAV] bridges defeq for rw; dif_neg (not if_neg) for dependent if-then-else; simp only [reflectSite_interface_self] handles proof-term transport where rw fails. See §8.11.37.\",\"id\":\"88\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-06 session 34): CRITICAL FINDING (§8.11.38) — character expansion gives ∑ A² (NOT ∑ |A|²), which is a FUNDAMENTAL obstacle. The σ twist conjugates the CHARACTER (χ→conj(χ)), NOT the COEFFICIENT (C→conj(C)). Character orthogonality gives δ_{αβ}, surviving term is A_α·A_α=A_α² (NOT |A_α|²). Dual pairing (A_{dual(α)}=conj(A_α)) only helps for self-dual characters; non-self-dual terms can be negative. Matrix element approach also fails: CG decomposition gives C_{α,j,i}≠conj(C_{α,i,j}). PD property of B_full gives χ_γ(V⁺) (not conj(χ_γ(V⁺))) — double conjugation cancels. CONCLUSION: character/matrix element expansion CANNOT prove integral ≥0. Lüscher mechanism likely uses FOSS SPACE construction. Build GREEN (unchanged, 2972 jobs). No code changes — pure analysis.\",\"id\":\"89\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"DONE (2026-08-06 session 35): KEY BREAKTHROUGH (§8.11.39) — Single-step transfer matrix kernel IS PD via gauge-fixing + character expansion. The kernel K_temporal(u_s,v_s) = ∑_γ (|c_γ|²/d_γ) χ_γ(W(0)·W(1)) where W(x)=v_s(x)·u_s(x)⁻¹. This is PD because |c_γ|²/d_γ ≥ 0 and characters are PD. PROOF MECHANISM: (1) Gauge-fix temporal links (temporal axial gauge u_t(0)=e), reducing to gauge-invariant variables v(x)=u_t(x+1)⁻¹·u_t(x). (2) Constraint ∏v(x)=e enforced by delta function, expanded in characters δ(g)=∑d_γ χ_γ(g). (3) Schur orthogonality gives non-negative coefficients |c_γ|²/d_γ. (4) Transfer matrix is self-adjoint (K(v,u)=conj(K(u,v))=K(u,v) since K is real). KEY OBSTACLE: reflection positivity has σ twist (u→u⁻¹) which changes v to v'≠v⁻¹ (non-abelian), creating 4-point functions. The σ twist is an ARTIFACT of reducing to ∫F·F(σ)dμ. Literature found: Osterwalder-Seiler(1978), BFS(1979) 'half gauge fields', Seiler(1982) lecture notes. Build GREEN (unchanged, 2972 jobs). No code changes — pure analysis.\",\"id\":\"90\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"IN PROGRESS: Prove the WEAKENED transferMatrixPositivity_axiom (now with dependsOnlyOnPosSpatialInterface). Step 1 (σ-disappears-from-g) DONE (session 33, item 88). Step 2 (shared-variable positivity) DONE (session 32, item 87). Step 3 (Lüscher mechanism) — KEY BREAKTHROUGH (session 35, item 90, §8.11.39): single-step transfer matrix kernel IS PD via gauge-fixing + character expansion (∑ |c_γ|²/d_γ · χ_γ ≥ 0). NEXT: (a) Read Seiler(1982) lecture notes for the actual proof mechanism handling the σ twist. (b) Study BFS 'half gauge fields' approach. (c) Formalize the single-step kernel PD property. (d) Reduce reflection positivity to single-step positivity (show ∫G·G(θU) = ⟨f,Tf⟩ for positive T). (e) Consider operator approach T=B*B. See §8.11.39 for full analysis.\",\"id\":\"79\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"PENDING: Assemble lemma 6 — close transferMatrixPositivity_axiom (axiom count 6→5). See §8.8. Requires proving the weakened axiom (item 79, via gauge-fixing + character expansion approach from §8.11.39).\",\"id\":\"48\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"pending\"}]}","name":"project_task_list"},"id":"e9f14ed8-fc01-493a-9d3f-198c418be33a","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":3009,"turn":0,"is_prune_marker":false}
