{"id":53,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean\n-- 1234 lines, 63175 bytes --\n1196 | lemma character_expansion_nonneg_shared\n1197 |     {X Z : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X] [MeasurableSpace Z]\n1198 |     (μ : Measure X) (ν : Measure Z) [SigmaFinite μ] [SigmaFinite ν]\n1199 |     (ι : Type*) [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n1200 |     (a : Z → ι → ℝ) (ha : ∀ z i, 0 ≤ a z i)\n1201 |     (Φ : ι → Z → X → ℂ) (g : X → Z → ℝ)\n1202 |     (hΦ_meas : ∀ i z, AEStronglyMeasurable (Φ i z) μ)\n1203 |     (hg_meas : ∀ z, AEStronglyMeasurable (fun x => (g x z : ℂ)) μ)\n1204 |     (hgΦ_int : ∀ z i, Integrable (fun x => (g x z : ℂ) * Φ i z x) μ)\n1205 |     (K : X → X → Z → ℂ)\n1206 |     (hK : ∀ x y z, K x y z = ∑ i, (a z i : ℂ) * (Φ i z x * conj (Φ i z y))) :\n1207 |     0 ≤ ∫ z, ∫ x, ∫ y, (g x z : ℂ) * (g y z : ℂ) * K x y z ∂μ ∂μ ∂ν := by\n1208 |   -- Pointwise: for each z, the inner double integral equals\n1209 |   -- ↑(∑ i, a z i * ‖∫ g(x,z)·Φ_i(z,x) dμ‖²) by character_expansion_positivity\n1210 |   -- with θ = id (so f(θ y) = f(y) = g(y,z)).\n1211 |   have heq : ∀ z,\n1212 |       (∫ x, ∫ y, (g x z : ℂ) * (g y z : ℂ) * K x y z ∂μ ∂μ) =\n1213 |         ↑(∑ i, a z i * ‖∫ x, (g x z : ℂ) * Φ i z x ∂μ‖^2) := by\n1214 |     intro z\n1215 |     exact character_expansion_positivity μ μ id (MeasurePreserving.id μ) ι (a z)\n1216 |       (fun i x => Φ i z x) (fun x => g x z) (fun i => hΦ_meas i z) (hg_meas z)\n1217 |       (fun i => hgΦ_int z i) (fun x y => K x y z) (fun x y => hK x y z)\n1218 |   -- Rewrite the outer integral using the pointwise (hence a.e.) equality.\n1219 |   rw [integral_congr_ae (ae_of_all ν heq)]\n1220 |   -- The pointwise equality produces `Complex.ofReal` coercions, while\n1221 |   -- `integral_ofReal` is stated with `RCLike.ofReal`; they are defeq\n1222 |   -- (`RCLike.ofReal_eq_complex_ofReal`) but not syntactically equal, so we\n1223 |   -- normalise the coercion first, then pull the `ofReal` out of the integral.\n1224 |   simp only [← RCLike.ofReal_eq_complex_ofReal]\n1225 |   rw [integral_ofReal]\n1226 |   -- The integral of a non-negative real function is non-negative.\n1227 |   apply Complex.zero_le_real.mpr\n1228 |   apply integral_nonneg\n1229 |   intro z\n1230 |   apply Finset.sum_nonneg\n1231 |   intro i _\n1232 |   exact mul_nonneg (ha z i) (sq_nonneg _)\n1233 | \n1234 | end YangMills\n\nTime: 2026-08-06 04:52:14 UTC","timestamp":1785991934,"token_count":731,"tool_call_id":"6b494f98-804b-4839-bf5a-be502bfcb722","full_token_estimate":536,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":1234,"byte_count":63175,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":28,"edit_line":null},"turn":29,"is_prune_marker":false}
