{"id":66,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 2697 lines, 157635 bytes --\n494 | noncomputable def wilsonActionOSPositive (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n495 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n496 |   ∑ n : PeriodicSite T L, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n497 |     if signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n498 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n499 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0 then\n500 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n501 |     else 0\n502 | \n503 | /-- The sum over all oriented plaquettes (n; μ, ν) where all four corners have\n504 | negative signed time. This is the correct negative-time part of the\n505 | Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition. -/\n506 | noncomputable def wilsonActionOSNegative (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n507 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n508 |   ∑ n : PeriodicSite T L, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n509 |     if signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n510 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n511 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0 then\n512 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n513 |     else 0\n514 | \n515 | /-- The sum over the remaining oriented plaquettes (those with corners on both sides\n516 | of the time interface). This is the interface part of the\n517 | Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition. -/\n518 | noncomputable def wilsonActionOSInterface (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n519 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n520 |   ∑ n : PeriodicSite T L, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n521 |     if ¬ (signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n522 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n523 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0) ∧\n524 |        ¬ (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n525 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n526 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0) then\n527 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n528 |     else 0\n529 | \n530 | /--\n531 | For each oriented plaquette (n; μ, ν), exactly one of the three conditions holds:\n532 | positive (all corners > 0), negative (all corners < 0), or interface (the rest).\n533 | -/\n\n... 2164 more line(s) below (use offset=534 to continue reading)\nTime: 2026-08-06 05:05:16 UTC","timestamp":1785992716,"token_count":821,"tool_call_id":"324eac21-cbbe-4ac3-b02c-da7fc653e99c","full_token_estimate":569,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":2697,"byte_count":157635,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":37,"is_prune_marker":false}
{"id":67,"role":"Assistant","content":"I'm at 75% context. Let me document the key findings and prepare for handoff. I've made a crucial discovery about the proof structure.\nTime: 2026-08-06 05:07:47 UTC","timestamp":1785992867,"token_count":40,"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"task_items\":[{\"content\":\"Analyze the proof gap: what's between integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg (proven) and ∫g·(Tg)≥0 (needed)\",\"id\":\"1\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Read character_expansion_nonneg_shared to check if it's the missing Lüscher piece\",\"id\":\"2\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Search for Seiler (1982) lecture notes online\",\"id\":\"3\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Document findings in design doc §8.11.40 and handoff\",\"id\":\"4\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"}],\"action\":\"update\"}","name":"todo_list"},"id":"bbf0d92d-10ac-4423-a690-33b29a523ca0","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":1659,"reasoning_content":"I'm at 75% context. Let me now understand the key finding and document it.\n\nFrom the definition of `wilsonActionOSPositive` (line 494-501):\n- S⁺ sums over plaquettes where ALL FOUR corners have signedTime > 0 (strictly positive time)\n- This means plaquettes at t=0 (the interface) are NOT in S⁺ — they're in S_int\n- The temporal links at t=0 (u⁰_t) connect t=0 to t=1, so plaquettes involving them have corners at t=0 and t=1, which are NOT all > 0\n- Therefore S⁺ does NOT depend on u⁰_t (temporal interface links)!\n\nThis is a CRUCIAL finding. It means:\n- A_w(u⁰) = ∫_{V⁺} g(merge(V⁺, u⁰)) · exp(-β·S⁺(merge(V⁺, u⁰))/2) · charFactorPos(w, V⁺) ∂μ⁺\n- Since g doesn't depend on u⁰_t (dependsOnlyOnPosSpatialInterface) and S⁺ doesn't depend on u⁰_t (all plaquettes have strictly positive time corners), A_w only depends on u⁰_s (spatial interface links)\n\nThis means the u⁰_t integral of charFactorInt(w, u⁰) gives a delta function (by character orthogonality), selecting w(l) = trivial for all temporal interface links l.\n\nSo the sum collapses to w with w(l) = trivial for temporal links, and the remaining integral is over u⁰_s, V⁺, V'⁺.\n\nBut the remaining question is: is the resulting kernel non-negative? The kernel is:\nK(V⁺, V'⁺, u⁰_s) = C · ∑_{w: w(l)=trivial for temporal l} F(w) · charFactorInt_spatial(w, u⁰_s) · charFactorPos(w, V⁺) · charFactorPos(w*, V'⁺)\n\nThis is still a sum with complex coefficients (characters), not non-negative reals. So `character_expansion_nonneg_shared` doesn't directly apply.\n\nThe Lüscher mechanism (gauge-fixing + delta function expansion + Schur orthogonality) is needed to get non-negative coefficients. This is the remaining hard part.\n\nLet me now document this finding and hand off. I have enough context to write a comprehensive handoff.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider. The key insight is that S⁺ doesn't depend on u⁰_t. This means the u⁰_t integral is JUST the character orthogonality of charFactorInt. But the S_int term DOES depend on u⁰_t (it involves plaquettes at the interface, which include temporal links at t=0).\n\nIn the `transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect` lemma, the character expansion is of exp(-β·S_int), not exp(-β·S⁺). So the charFactorInt(w, u⁰) comes from the S_int expansion, and it involves characters of ALL interface links (both spatial and temporal).\n\nThe u⁰_t integral of charFactorInt(w, u⁰) · [rest of the integrand that doesn't depend on u⁰_t] gives a delta function by character orthogonality.\n\nBut wait — the S_int term is ALREADY expanded in characters (that's what h_char does). The charFactorInt(w, u⁰) is the character factor from the interface links. So the u⁰_t integral of charFactorInt(w, u⁰) gives δ_{w(l), trivial} for temporal links l.\n\nBut the S⁺ term is NOT expanded in characters — it's in the exp(-β·S⁺/2) factor inside A_w. Since S⁺ doesn't depend on u⁰_t, the exp(-β·S⁺/2) factor doesn't depend on u⁰_t, so it factors out of the u⁰_t integral.\n\nSo the u⁰_t integral gives:\n∫_{u⁰_t} charFactorInt(w, u⁰) ∂μ⁰_t = ∏_{l ∈ temporal interface} δ_{w(l), trivial}\n\nAnd the sum collapses to w with w(l) = trivial for temporal links.\n\nFor these w, the remaining integral is:\nC · ∑_{w: temporal trivial} F(w) · ∫_{u⁰_s} charFactorInt_spatial(w, u⁰_s) · A_{w*}(u⁰_s) · A_w(u⁰_s) ∂μ⁰_s\n\nNow, the key question: is F(w) ≥ 0 for w with w(l) = trivial for temporal links?\n\nF(w) is the character expansion coefficient of the Boltzmann factor exp(-β·S_int). The S_int involves plaquettes at the interface, which couple temporal links u⁰_t with spatial links. After the character expansion, F(w) is the coefficient for the character configuration w.\n\nIf w(l) = trivial for temporal links, then the temporal link characters are trivial (χ_trivial = 1). The remaining characters are for spatial interface links. The coefficient F(w) for such w involves the character expansion of the Boltzmann factor with trivial temporal characters.\n\nHmm, but F(w) is still a complex number in general (it's a character expansion coefficient). The non-negativity of F(w) is NOT guaranteed.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider the Lüscher mechanism more carefully. The key insight from session 35 is:\n\nThe single-step kernel K_temporal(u_s, v_s) = ∑_γ (|c_γ|²/d_γ) χ_γ(W(0)·W(1)) where W(x) = v_s(x)·u_s(x)⁻¹.\n\nThis is PD because |c_γ|²/d_γ ≥ 0 and χ_γ is PD.\n\nThe key difference from the current code: the Lüscher mechanism uses the delta function expansion (constraint ∏ v(x) = e), which gives d_γ χ_γ, and Schur orthogonality gives |c_γ|²/d_γ. The current code uses the Boltzmann factor expansion, which gives F(w) (not necessarily non-negative).\n\nSo the Lüscher mechanism is a DIFFERENT character expansion — it expands the delta function, not the Boltzmann factor. The delta function expansion gives d_γ χ_γ (with d_γ > 0), and Schur orthogonality gives |c_γ|²/d_γ ≥ 0.\n\nThe current code's character expansion (h_char in `transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect`) expands the Boltzmann factor exp(-β·S_int), not the delta function. So the coefficients F(w) are NOT necessarily non-negative.\n\nTo use the Lüscher mechanism, we need to:\n1. Gauge-fix the temporal links (temporal axial gauge u⁰_t = e)\n2. This introduces a delta function (constraint from periodic BC)\n3. Expand the delta function in characters: δ(g) = ∑_γ d_γ χ_γ(g)\n4. Apply Schur orthogonality to get |c_γ|²/d_γ ≥ 0\n\nThis is a DIFFERENT approach from the current code's character expansion of the Boltzmann factor.\n\nOK, I think I've now fully understood the situation. Let me document this and hand off.\n\nThe key findings of this session:\n1. S⁺ does NOT depend on u⁰_t (temporal interface links) — confirmed from the definition (all plaquettes have strictly positive time corners)\n2. `character_expansion_nonneg_shared` is the RIGHT non-negativity lemma, but it requires non-negative coefficients\n3. The current code's character expansion (of the Boltzmann factor) gives complex coefficients F(w), NOT non-negative\n4. The Lüscher mechanism (gauge-fixing + delta function expansion + Schur orthogonality) gives non-negative coefficients |c_γ|²/d_γ, but it's a DIFFERENT approach that hasn't been formalized\n5. The proof structure is: ∫ G·G(θU) = ∫ g·(Tg) → σ-invisibility → u⁰_t integral (character orthogonality) → Lüscher mechanism (non-negative kernel) → `character_expansion_nonneg_shared` → ≥ 0\n\nThe remaining work:\n1. Formalize the gauge-fixing of temporal links (temporal axial gauge)\n2. Formalize the delta function expansion (constraint ∏ v(x) = e)\n3. Apply Schur orthogonality to get non-negative coefficients |c_γ|²/d_γ\n4. Show the resulting kernel matches the form of `character_expansion_nonneg_shared`\n5. Apply `character_expansion_nonneg_shared` to get ∫ g·(Tg) ≥ 0\n6. Close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`\n\nLet me now write the design doc update and hand off.","turn":39,"is_prune_marker":false}
