{"id":75,"role":"Assistant","content":"","timestamp":1785993410,"token_count":0,"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"reason\":\"Context at 80%. Completed analysis session documenting the complete 6-step proof structure and identifying the precise remaining gap (Lüscher mechanism formalization). No code changes this session — pure analysis. Build GREEN (2972 jobs).\",\"next_prompt\":\"You are continuing the YangMills Lean 4 formalization project (goal: close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`, axiom count 6→5). Read `project_task_list` first.\\n\\n## Current state (session 36 → 37)\\n\\n**BUILD IS GREEN** (2972 jobs). All code compiles. 0 sorries, 0 new custom axioms.\\n\\n### KEY FINDING from session 36 (§8.11.40 in design doc)\\n\\n**S⁺ does NOT depend on u⁰_t (temporal interface links).** Confirmed from `wilsonActionOSPositive` definition (ReflectionPositivity.lean:494-501): S⁺ sums over plaquettes where ALL FOUR corners have `signedTime > 0` (strictly positive time). Temporal interface links u⁰_t connect t=0 to t=1, so plaquettes involving them have corners at t=0 — NOT all strictly positive. These plaquettes are in S_int, NOT S⁺.\\n\\nThis session clarified the COMPLETE 6-step proof structure for closing `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`:\\n\\n1. **∫ G·G(θU) = ∫ g·(Tg)** — PROVEN (`integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg`, TransferMatrix.lean:4936). Reduces reflection positivity to showing T is a positive operator.\\n\\n2. **σ disappears from g** — PROVEN (`g_posInterface_sigma_invisible`, TransferMatrix.lean:1986). With `dependsOnlyOnPosSpatialInterface`, g(mergePosInterface(V⁺, σ(u⁰))) = g(mergePosInterface(V⁺, u⁰)).\\n\\n3. **Character expansion of T** — PROVEN (`transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect`, TransferMatrix.lean:5792). Gives: ∫ ψ·T(ψ) = C · ∑_w F(w) · ∫_{u⁰} charFactorInt(w, u⁰) · A_{w*}(σ(u⁰)) · A_w(u⁰) ∂μ⁰ where A_w = fourierCoeffPos(w, ·), w* = fullReflectReindex(w).\\n\\n4. **σ-invisibility of A_{w*}** — From step 2, A_{w*}(σ(u⁰)) = A_{w*}(u⁰) (since A involves g and S⁺, both σ-invisible). So: ∫ ψ·T(ψ) = C · ∑_w F(w) · ∫_{u⁰} charFactorInt(w, u⁰) · A_{w*}(u⁰) · A_w(u⁰) ∂μ⁰\\n\\n5. **u⁰_t integral via character orthogonality** — Since A_w and A_{w*} don't depend on u⁰_t (g doesn't depend on u⁰_t by hypothesis; S⁺ doesn't depend on u⁰_t by the finding above), the u⁰_t integral of charFactorInt(w, u⁰) gives δ_{w(l), trivial} for temporal interface links l. The sum collapses to w with w(l) = trivial for temporal links.\\n\\n6. **Non-negativity of the remaining kernel** — THE REMAINING GAP. The kernel K(V⁺, V'⁺, u⁰_s) = C · ∑_w F(w) · charFactorInt_spatial(w, u⁰_s) · charFactorPos(w, V⁺) · charFactorPos(w*, V'⁺) needs to be shown ≥ 0 when integrated against g·g. **OBSTACLE:** The coefficients F(w) · charFactorInt_spatial(w, u⁰_s) are COMPLEX (characters are complex), NOT non-negative reals. So `character_expansion_nonneg_shared` (PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean:1196) does NOT directly apply — it requires a(z,i) ≥ 0.\\n\\n### The solution: The Lüscher mechanism (from §8.11.39)\\n\\nThe current code's character expansion (h_char in `transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect`) expands the BOLTZMANN FACTOR exp(-β·S_int), giving complex coefficients F(w). The Lüscher mechanism instead:\\n- (a) Gauge-fixes temporal links (temporal axial gauge u⁰_t = e)\\n- (b) Introduces a delta function (constraint ∏ v(x) = e from periodic BC)\\n- (c) Expands the delta function in characters: δ(g) = ∑_γ d_γ χ_γ(g) (with d_γ > 0)\\n- (d) Applies Schur orthogonality to get non-negative coefficients |c_γ|²/d_γ ≥ 0\\n- (e) The resulting kernel K = ∑_γ (|c_γ|²/d_γ) χ_γ(W(0)·W(1)) is PD\\n\\nThis is a DIFFERENT character expansion from the current code's approach. The Lüscher mechanism has NOT been formalized yet.\\n\\n### `character_expansion_nonneg_shared` (PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean:1196) — the key non-negativity lemma\\n\\nIf K(x,y,z) = ∑_i a(z,i) · Φ_i(z,x) · conj(Φ_i(z,y)) with a(z,i) ≥ 0, then ∫∫∫ g(x,z)·g(y,z)·K(x,y,z) dμ(x) dμ(y) dν(z) ≥ 0. This is because the inner double integral equals ∑_i a(z,i) · |∫ g(x,z)·Φ_i(z,x) dμ|² ≥ 0. This lemma IS the right tool for the final step — once the Lüscher mechanism provides non-negative coefficients.\\n\\n### Remaining work to close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`\\n\\n1. Formalize the gauge-fixing of temporal links (temporal axial gauge u⁰_t = e)\\n2. Formalize the delta function expansion (constraint ∏ v(x) = e): δ(g) = ∑_γ d_γ χ_γ(g)\\n3. Apply Schur orthogonality to get non-negative coefficients |c_γ|²/d_γ\\n4. Show the resulting kernel K(V⁺, V'⁺, u⁰_s) = ∑_γ (|c_γ|²/d_γ) · Φ_γ(u⁰_s, V⁺) · conj(Φ_γ(u⁰_s, V'⁺)) matches the form of `character_expansion_nonneg_shared`\\n5. Apply `character_expansion_nonneg_shared` to get ∫ g·(Tg) ≥ 0\\n6. Combine with `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` to close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`\\n\\n### Key infrastructure already available\\n- `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` (TransferMatrix.lean:4936) — reduces ∫ G·G(θU) to ∫ g·(Tg)\\n- `g_posInterface_sigma_invisible` (TransferMatrix.lean:1986) — σ disappears from g\\n- `transfer_matrix_fubini_integrated_pull_fullReflect` (TransferMatrix.lean:5792) — character expansion of T\\n- `character_expansion_nonneg_shared` (PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean:1196) — non-negativity lemma (PROVEN, 0 sorries)\\n- `plaquetteBoltzmannPD` / `plaquetteBoltzmannPD_inv` (PeterWeyl.lean:325/425) — PD of plaquette factors\\n- `characterOrthogonality` (PeterWeyl.lean) — Schur orthogonality for matrix elements\\n- `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette` (PeterWeyl.lean) — axiom providing ι, ρ, cgME, hcgME_decomp, hcgME_unitary\\n- `interfaceLinkTemporal` / `interfaceLinkSpatial` (TransferMatrix.lean) — split of interface links by μ=0 vs μ≠0\\n- `sigmaInterface_apply` (TransferMatrix.lean) — σ inverts temporal μ=0, keeps spatial μ≠0\\n\\n### Key files & line numbers\\n- `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` — ReflectionPositivity.lean:2476 (the axiom to close)\\n- `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive` — ReflectionPositivity.lean:2491 (uses the axiom at line 2576)\\n- `wilsonActionOSPositive` — ReflectionPositivity.lean:494 (S⁺ definition — confirmed NOT depending on u⁰_t)\\n- `osPositiveOfPosInterface` — TransferMatrix.lean:1245 (S⁺ for PosInterfaceConfig)\\n- `transferMatrixCorrect` — TransferMatrix.lean:1279 (the transfer matrix T)\\n- `transferMatrixReflected` — TransferMatrix.lean:2459 (T after change of variables)\\n- `G` — TransferMatrix.lean:1307 (G(U) = f(U)·exp(-β·S⁺)·exp(-β·S_int/2))\\n- `g_posInterface` — TransferMatrix.lean:1327 (g(u) = f(u)·exp(-β·S⁺/2))\\n- `charFactorPos` / `charFactorInt` / `charFactorNeg` — TransferMatrix.lean:2268/2282/2296\\n- `fourierCoeffPos` / `fourierCoeffNeg` — TransferMatrix.lean:4627/4645\\n- `fullReflectReindex` — TransferMatrix.lean:5536 (w* definition)\\n\\n### Build commands\\n- Windows build: `powershell -Command \\\"lake build YangMills.Proofs.TransferMatrix 2>&1 | Select-String -Pattern 'error:|Build completed' | Select-Object -Last 10\\\"`\\n- Full build: `powershell -Command \\\"lake build 2>&1 | Select-String -Pattern 'error:|Build completed' | Select-Object -Last 10\\\"`\\n\\n### Suggested first actions for session 37\\n\\nThe MOST PROMISING next step is to formalize the Lüscher mechanism. This is a significant formalization effort. Start by:\\n\\n1. **Study the existing character expansion infrastructure** in PeterWeyl.lean — look at `plaquetteBoltzmannPD`, `characterOrthogonality`, `peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette`, and the character expansion lemmas. Understand what's available for expanding functions in characters and applying Schur orthogonality.\\n\\n2. **Formalize the delta function expansion** δ(g) = ∑_γ d_γ χ_γ(g). This is the Peter-Weyl theorem for the delta function. Check if Mathlib has this or if it needs to be built from `characterOrthogonality`.\\n\\n3. **Formalize the gauge-fixing** (temporal axial gauge u⁰_t = e). This is a change of variables that fixes the temporal links. The key is that the Haar measure is invariant under this gauge-fixing (Faddeev-Popov determinant = 1 for axial gauge).\\n\\n4. **Apply Schur orthogonality** to compute the u⁰_t integral after gauge-fixing, getting non-negative coefficients |c_γ|²/d_γ.\\n\\n5. **Connect to `character_expansion_nonneg_shared`** — show the resulting kernel has the form K(x,y,z) = ∑_i a(z,i) · Φ_i(z,x) · conj(Φ_i(z,y)) with a ≥ 0.\\n\\nAlternatively, consider whether the Seiler (1982) lecture notes (doi:10.1007/3-540-11559-5, available behind paywall on Springer) can be accessed through other means, as they contain the most accessible description of the proof mechanism.\"}","name":"handoff"},"id":"fbd0f84f-85bc-45fc-b800-facb3b69174d","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":1768,"reasoning_content":"I'm at 80% context. Let me hand off now with a comprehensive briefing for the next session.","turn":45,"is_prune_marker":false}
